{
  "id": "COMPOUND:42780 - PROTEIN:6326",
  "verbalization": "Crassumolide D is shown to interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which is a key component of the polycomb repressive complex 2 (PRC2). This complex is known to regulate gene expression by methylating histone H3 lysine 27, and it is a well-documented target of 2,4,6-trihydroxy-3-(3,3-dimethylallyl)acetophenone, a compound that inhibits PDE6C. The evidence from multiple paths indicates that Crassumolide D, through its interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, leads to the inhibition of PDE6C. The consistent pathway from Crassumolide D to PDE6C, via multiple distinct metabolites of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, suggests a mechanistic link that is supported by the scores assigned to each path. The overlapping targets and the shared interaction with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex provide a robust foundation for the proposed relationship. The integration of these pathways supports the idea that Crassumolide D may act as a modulator of PDE6C through a mechanism involving the polycomb repressive complex 2.",
